                <pb facs="0808" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.6363 Manchuria/23: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-14T12:00:00+08:00">July 14,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received July 14—7:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>304. Department’s 112, July 5, 6 p.m. to Tokyo regarding petroleum monopoly.
                    British Legation informs me that British Consulate [at] Mukden has now been
                    instructed to make representations to Vice Minister for Foreign Affairs at
                    Hsinching leaving with him an unaddressed memorandum in the sense of item (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">e</hi>) of Tokyo’s 142, July 3, 6 p.m. to the
                    Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
